# ROMs awaiting a Stella capture.
#
# Capturing needs Stella's GUI: the write-only TIA registers live only in the
# debugger's TIA tab, and driving it means bringing Stella to the front and sending
# keystrokes, which takes over the user's screen for ~13 s per ROM. That is not
# something to do in the middle of someone's working session, so a ROM added while
# the machine is in use is queued here and captured in a batch later.
#
# THIS FILE IS NOT AN EXEMPTION LIST. The test prints every line on every run and
# fails once the queue passes maxQueuedCaptures, so a queue that stops being drained
# becomes louder rather than quieter. A permanently uncoverable ROM does not belong
# here — it belongs in a named exclusion with a reason.
#
# Format: <rom path>  # YYYY-MM-DD  why it is queued rather than captured
# Drain with: scripts/stella_oracle.sh <rom> 5 tia   (then delete the line)
roms/litmus/litmus_vdel_bits.bin  # 2026-09-07 — VDELPx bit decode (bit 0 only; $FE behaves as $00)
roms/litmus/litmus_tim64t_zero.bin  # 2026-09-07 — TIM64T countdown length (2692 cy, not 43*64)
roms/litmus/litmus_pal_physics.bin  # 2026-09-07 — NTSC/PAL per-frame identity (physics scaling)
roms/litmus/litmus_store7_overrun.bin  # 2026-09-07 — negative control: prover certifies, frame is 269 lines
roms/litmus/litmus_bank_capacity.bin  # 2026-09-07 — stores per line at three bank-reach costs
roms/litmus/litmus_hmp0_vs_hmp1.bin  # 2026-09-07 — HMP0/HMP1 symmetry across all 16 nibbles
roms/litmus/litmus_player_missile_9px.bin  # 2026-09-07 — 8px player + 1px missile = one 9px shape
roms/litmus/litmus_counter_entropy.bin  # 2026-09-07 — where a free-running counter's randomness comes from
